WEBVTT

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:35.140
Taebaek refers to the Han people's holy Baekdu mountain and Venus that lights the day early in the morning.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:52.100
The progress line of Taebaek Pumsae, which represents the will of Venus to light the whole world through Taekwondo, is the character Gom, which means artisan.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:56.300
We will now take a look at the key moves of Taebaek Pumsae.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:02:14.220
Taebaek Pumsae consists of five key moves, namely Bomseogi Sonnal Arae Haecheomagi, Sonnal Oppo Japgi, Geumgang Pakkatmakgi, Turobaegi, and Deungjumeok Pakkachigi.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:26.620
We will now take a closer look at each of the key moves of Taebaek Pumsae.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:34.620
When performing Bomseogi Sonnal Arae Haecheomagi, both hands should be placed in the center line of the thigh of the front leg.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:42.620
The back of your hands should each face outward and the space between your hand and body should be about one hand's length sideways.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:46.620
Start in front of your chest and perform Haecheomagi downward.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:53.620
When assuming postures where the legs are spread forwards and backwards like Bomseogi and Apgubi,

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:58.620
the arm on the same side as the front foot should cross from the outside.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:02.620
For Sonnal Oppo Japgi, assume an opponent has hold of you.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:05.620
Twist the thumb of the hand being held outside.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:09.620
Then open your hand so the palm is seen from above.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.620
Raise your hand and pull it close to your body to release your wrist.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:18.620
Open your arm inside out and cover the back of the hand of your opponent.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:21.620
Hold, bend back, and pull.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:27.620
While bending and twisting, be careful not to let your elbow rise excessively or move outward

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:33.620
as you can only exert force effectively when the elbow is close to the torso.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:41.620
For Geumgang Bakalmaki, start with Jangun Doljakui and move together to the center line.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:45.620
This is a technique where the outer arm performs Olgulmaki

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:50.620
and the inner arm performs Anpalmok Bakalmaki at the same time.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:55.620
Turoppegi is a technique where you spin the thumb toward the inner wrist

00:03:55.620 --> 00:04:00.870
and release between an opponent's thumb and index finger.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:05.870
When performing Olgulpakachigi, strengthen the shoulder and shoulder blade

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:09.870
by bending the elbow and utilize the torque of the torso.

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:15.870
The elbow should face downward and the fist raised level with the temple.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:18.870
Be careful not to bend the elbow.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:22.870
These are the five key moves of Taebaek Pumsae.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:27.870
We will now look at the moves in succession connecting each move.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:31.870
The key moves of Taebaek first part consist of

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:54.180
and

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:03.880
When performing Taebaek's first move,

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.880
move your center to your right foot.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:10.880
Set your left foot to the left and assume the Wenbomseogi posture.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:13.880
When blocking from the Wenbomseogi posture,

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:16.880
the left arm should cross on the outside.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:20.880
The Aptagi should be performed forward in a straight line.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.880
The kicking foot is folded after the kick.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.880
The ball should touch the ground first,

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:31.880
then complete your breath and move the moment your heel touches the ground.

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:34.880
When performing Momtongdobuljirugi,

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:39.880
the lower body should be planted firm to maintain balance.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:41.880
When performing Jochonegi,

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:45.880
pull the hand close to the body and release the wrist

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:49.880
or perform Jirugi by brushing aside and setting your right foot.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:54.880
Jochonegi and Jirugi should be performed naturally in succession.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:06:00.800
Cautions for Taebaek first part, taking a closer look.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:08.050
Be mindful of the inner and outer location of the arm when starting Hechomaki.

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:14.450
During Aptagi, with the upper body fixed in place,

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:17.450
do not kick using only the legs.

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:22.450
Be careful not to let the elbow open when performing Jirugi.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:28.080
When performing Jeppipumanchigi,

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:33.080
do not twist the torso excessively and lose balance or swerve to the right.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:58.060
We will now practice the moves of Taebaek first part in succession while watching the video.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:01.060
The key moves of Taebaek second part consist of

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:16.060
When performing Dangyojirugi,

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:21.060
the hammer fist being pulled must not touch the front of the opposite shoulder.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:25.060
Pull the left foot to the inside of the right knee.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:28.060
Move your center to the right foot.

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:31.060
When performing Jeppipumanchigi,

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:36.060
do not twist the torso excessively and lose balance or swerve to the right.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:42.460
Do not twist the torso excessively and lose balance or swerve to the left.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:45.460
Move your center to the right foot.

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:49.460
Then complete Orenhakdariseogi Orenjageundoljageui.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:54.900
When performing Wenyopchagi Orenpalgupyojeokchigi,

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:59.900
leave the right fist on the back in the Jageundoljageui posture.

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:06.900
The left fist should start from the waist and draw a circle inside out to perform the Yeopchagi.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:10.900
Your arms and legs should be parallel above and below.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:16.540
Cautions for Taebaek second part, taking a closer look.

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:21.540
When performing Geumgangbakkatmakgi, do not block after crossing your arms.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:26.540
Be careful not to let the Dangyojirugi become Chijirugi.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:31.540
Do not perform Jirugi while the opposite arm is fixed.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:37.540
When pulling the left foot from the Orendikgupy while performing Orenjageundoljageui,

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:40.540
be careful not to straighten the supporting right knee.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:43.540
It is important to maintain the same elevation.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:47.540
During Wenyopchagi Orenpalgupyojeokchigi,

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:52.540
do not perform Yeopchagi by crossing your arms in front of your chest.

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:58.540
We will now practice the moves of Taebaek second part in succession while watching the video.

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:18.570
The key moves to Taebaek third part consist of

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:21.570
Wensonalgeodeuromakgi

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:24.570
Orensongkeutsewojjirugi

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:26.570
One hand Mitorobegi

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:28.570
Dungjumokpakachigi

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:31.570
and Orenjirugi

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:34.570
When performing Wensonalgeodeuromakgi,

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:42.040
the hand blade should be level with the solar plexus and the elbow should point downward.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:47.040
The elbow of the blocking arm should maintain 90 degrees to 120 degrees

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:52.040
and the assisting left hand should be level with the right elbow.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:55.040
Keep the left elbow close to the body

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:59.040
and leave one hand length between the outer wrist and torso.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:03.450
When performing Seongkutsewojirugi,

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:09.450
keep the index, middle and ring finger in a straight line at the same length to prevent injuries.

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:14.450
The force is concentrated in the tip of the hand with a small area of contact,

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:18.450
making it effective in attacking the opponent's pressure points.

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:20.450
When performing Mitorobegi,

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:23.450
you must move and set the left foot to the left.

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:28.450
Twist the body to the opposite direction of progress, then perform Wenapgubi.

00:10:28.450 --> 00:10:31.450
Place your left hand in front of the chest.

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:35.450
Open your hand with a space of one raised fist.

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:40.450
Open your right hand and pull the back of your hand to the right back.

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:43.450
Begi must be performed quickly.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:47.450
Use your arm and weight together to finish the move.

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:49.450
Push off the ground with the left foot.

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:51.450
Move your center to the right foot.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:54.450
Spin with the right ball as an axis.

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:57.450
Then perform Dungjumokbakachigi.

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:01.450
Orenjirugi is performed with a shout.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:07.360
Perform Nedikgi with Orenapgubi,

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:13.360
following the previous Orendikgubi Dungjumokchigi with no change in elevation.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:19.920
Cautions for Taebaek 3rd part, taking a closer look.

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:25.380
When performing Sonagoduromaki,

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:28.380
the elbow should not move forward.

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:36.190
If it does, the direction of the force will change.

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:39.190
When performing Sonkutsewojirugi,

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:42.190
be careful not to let the wrist bend.

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:44.190
When performing Mituropegi,

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:49.890
do not pull by merely changing directions.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.890
When performing Dungjumokbakachigi,

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:54.890
be careful not to let the wrist bend.

00:11:54.890 --> 00:12:01.170
We will now practice the moves of Taebaek 3rd part in succession while watching the video.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:16.210
The key moves of Taebaek 4th part consist of

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:22.210
Orenkawimaki, Orenaptagi, and Doubujirugi.

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:28.650
Wenkawimaki, Wenaptagi, and Doubujirugi.

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:34.650
Kawimaki is a technique to perform Aremaki and Anpalmokbakkatmaki simultaneously,

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:41.650
but it can also be utilized as a more appropriate technique depending on the motion.

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:45.650
Cautions for Taebaek 4th part, taking a closer look.

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:52.650
The basics of Kawimaki is to perform Aremaki with the left arm when the left foot is in front,

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:56.650
and Anpalmokbakkatmaki with the right arm.

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:58.650
When performing Aptagi,

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:04.650
be careful not to let the kicking leg pass the supporting leg and do a folding kick.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:23.220
We will now practice the moves of Taebaek 4th part in succession while watching the video.

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:26.220
This concludes the training for Taebaek Pumsae.

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:30.220
We will take another look at all the moves and master Pumsae.

00:13:30.220 --> 00:14:33.070
We have looked at all the key moves of Taebaek Pumsae

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:38.070
and provided thorough explanations for each move and things to watch out for.

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:42.070
Continue with your training of Taebaek which seeks to light the world

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:46.070
and let the light abide in your body and mind as well.

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:49.070
We will see you again in the Pyeongwon Pumsae video.

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:51.070
Thanks for watching.

